course: dictionary
lesson: 15681
title: A word from the falconry field
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one special hobby or sport. Falconry is the old sport of training hawks and falcons to hunt. Inside that world, people use a special word for the male bird: tiercel. «The falconer watched the tiercel swoop down on the rabbit.» The clues are falconer, hawks and hunt, so tiercel must be a kind of bird.
explain: Tiercel is a noun, so it names a thing. Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word: «The falconer watched the male bird swoop down on the rabbit.» It still makes sense, so tiercel means a male hawk or falcon.
explain: Tiercel can also be spelled tercel, and both spellings mean the same thing. You may see it in old stories, bird books and poems, so keep an eye out for it. When you meet a word like this, a dictionary is a good friend.
fact: A tiercel is a male hawk or falcon.
fact: Tiercel can also be spelled tercel.
fact: Falconry is the sport of training hawks and falcons to hunt.
fact: «The tiercel is about a third smaller than the female.» The name comes from an old word for third.
fact: You may see phrases such as «a tiercel peregrine» and «falcon and tiercel».
exercise: «The falconer whistled, and the tiercel flew back to her glove.» What does tiercel mean? | A type of old castle wall | *A male hawk or falcon | A female falcon | A small fish that lives in rivers
exercise: «Tom saw a falcon and its tiercel perched on the old tower.» Which bird is the tiercel? | The fish on the riverbank | *The male bird | The bird's nest | The female bird
exercise: Another spelling of tiercel is which word? | tierce | teercel | *tercel | tiercet
test: Falconry is the sport of training hawks and falcons to hunt. What does falconry mean? | *Training hawks and falcons to hunt | Watching birds from a boat | Painting pictures of birds | Racing horses across open fields
test: «The tiercel is about a third smaller than the female.» Why does the word tiercel link to the word third? | It is the number of birds in a flock | It means the bird is very large | *The name comes from an old word for third | It means a group of three birds
exam: Which word means a male hawk or falcon, and can also be spelled tercel? | Mantle | Eyrie | *Tiercel | Falconry
